  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given integers NNN and KKK.\n\nFind a permutation PPP of length NNN such that:\n\n\n∑i=1N(max⁡j=1iPj−min⁡j=1iPj)=K\\sum_{i=1}^{N} ( \\max\\limits_{j = 1}^{i} P_j - \\min\\limits_{j = 1}^{i} P_j ) = K∑i=1N​(j=1maxi​Pj​−j=1mini​Pj​)=K\nIf there exists multiple PPP, you can print any one.\n\nOtherwise report that it is not possible.\n\nNote that a permutation of length NNN consists of all integers from 111 to NNN exactly once.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two positive integers NNN and KKK −-− the length of PPP and the required sum.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line −1-1−1 if there does not exist any such PPP.\nOtherwise, print NNN distinct positive integers, representing permutation PPP.\n\n\nIf there exists multiple PPP, you can print any one.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1061 \\leq T \\leq 10^61≤T≤106",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "0≤K≤N20 \\leq K \\leq N^20≤K≤N2",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 0\n1 1\n2 0\n3 4",
        "output": "1\n-1\n-1\n1 3 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: For the permutation [1][1][1], (max⁡j=11Pj−min⁡j=11Pj)=1−1=0(\\max\\limits_{j = 1}^{1} P_j - \\min\\limits_{j = 1}^{1} P_j) = 1-1 = 0(j=1max1​Pj​−j=1min1​Pj​)=1−1=0.\nTest case 222: The only permutation of length 111 gives the sum 000.\nTest case 333: It can be shown that no permutation of length 222 gives the sum 000.\nTest case 444: Consider the permutation [1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2].\nThe sum of difference between maximum and minimum in each prefix is (1−1)+(3−1)+(3−1)=4(1-1) + (3-1) + (3-1) = 4(1−1)+(3−1)+(3−1)=4."
      }
    ]
  },
